# Component behaviors

Declare platform patterns on each component `schema.yml` under `behaviors:` — do not invent parallel keys (`variant_behaviors`, etc.).

| Id | When to declare |
|----|-----------------|
| `conversion` | field-editors include `form-settings` |
| `listing` | `dynamic_entries` / listing cards |
| `schema_org` | SSR JSON-LD contributor |
| `ecommerce` | funnel/catalog events or `cta-tracking` / `ecommerce-products` field-editors |

## CTA tracking

CTA ecommerce intent is **not** on behaviors. Bind paths with field-editor type `cta-tracking`. Required `cta.tracking`: `none` | `add_to_cart` | `click_begin_checkout`.

Save/MCP validate bound paths (`validateCtaTracking` + `validateCtaPurchasable`). Non-`none` needs a purchasable product (`_ecommerce.yml`).

## Product scope (exact property paths)

Ecommerce product scope is field-editor / domain **bound paths** — not URL sniffing as the primary API.

| Component | Property path |
|-----------|---------------|
| `hero` course on program entry | inherit entry slug; optional `ecommerce_products` |
| `hero` course elsewhere | `ecommerce_products` (`string[]` \| `"all"`) |
| `enrollment_selector` | `programs[].id` (default); optional `ecommerce_products: all` for shared hubs |
| `pricing_plans` | inherit on program pages, or `ecommerce_products` |
| CTA intent | bound CTA path + `.tracking` (e.g. `signup_card.cta_button.tracking`) |

`explain_site` topics `component-behaviors` and `ecommerce` **must list these exact property paths** — never vague “set product scope” alone. Do not document a second parallel field that is not the bind.

Funnel order is **not** a section property — use `get_product_funnel` / `update_product_funnel` / `_ecommerce.yml` `funnel.steps` and `funnel.traffic_sources` (top-of-funnel types; not URL steps).

CMS does **not** manage a billing plan catalog.

## Wipe on duplicate (derived)

Page/section duplicate clears conversion/ecommerce identity fields (no `reset_on_duplicate` schema key):

- Any `conversion_name` under the section (including `routes[].conversion_name`)
- Whole `ecommerce_products`
- CTA `tracking` on bound `cta-tracking` paths (delete → save fails until re-set)

Not wiped (v1): `programs[].id`, automations/webhook/tags, ordinary props.

When adding a component: binding `form-settings`, `cta-tracking`, or `ecommerce-products` **implies** those values wipe on duplicate. Default for new props: do **not** wipe. Duplicate never fails; save/publish/**promote** validators require an explicit decision: missing keys fail; `conversion_name` / `ecommerce_products` use YAML `null` for off; CTA uses `tracking: none`. Empty string ≠ off.

Catalog: `docs/component-behaviors.md`. MCP: `explain_site` topics `component-behaviors` + `ecommerce`. Schema-sync **preserves** `behaviors`.
